id: hac-r17v
title: Add token-efficient registry discovery and release-runner parity
description: "Expose the official compact entity-registry display contract for agent workflows, preserve full typed and passthrough access, update the managed changelog package, and make tag-driven publication provision the same mandatory verifier toolchain as automatic release preparation."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 0
tags[8]: agents,api,entity-registry,github-actions,home-assistant,pm-changelog,release,websocket
created_at: "2026-07-24T21:01:24.761Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-24T21:41:13.785Z"
deadline: "2026-07-26T21:01:24.761Z"
assignee: codex-root
author: codex-root
estimated_minutes: 420
acceptance_criteria: "hassio registries exposes the official compact display endpoint with token-efficient and decoded output, filtering, count, and limit behavior; Full source coverage remains 100/100/100/100, docstrings remain complete, every command help path and every formatter remains valid, and live read-only E2E passes; Tag-driven publish installs every tool required by release:verify, latest pm-changelog generates the canonical changelog, and hosted rehearsal succeeds without publishing a new version"
definition_of_ready: "All-status PM lineage, official docs, live endpoint shape, exact failed release logs, current code, and managed package versions reviewed without recording private values"
goal: complete-agent-home-assistant-interface
objective: compact-discovery-and-reliable-publication
value: Reduce agent token and bandwidth cost while restoring trustworthy automated release verification.
impact: Agents can query enabled registry metadata efficiently and maintainers can trust the same mandatory gates in preparation and publication.
outcome: A reviewed and merged typed discovery surface with reproducible clean-runner release parity.
why_now: "The official compact endpoint is live but untyped in the CLI, and the latest production tag failed before publication because the publish runner omitted mandatory tools."
parent: hac-4s9j
reviewer: unbraind
risk: high
confidence: 96
sprint: 2026-07-compact-registry
release: 2026.7.24
