comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-24T21:01:24.761Z",codex-root,Duplicate audit found no existing compact list_for_display item; the open GitHub release blocker is the production manifestation of a distinct publish-runner tool provisioning gap.
  "2026-07-24T21:17:36.449Z",codex-root,"Implementation checkpoint: latest PM CLI 2026.7.24-3 confirmed; managed pm-changelog upgraded to 2026.7.23; focused tests, typecheck, lint, docstrings, file size, duplication, 100/100/100/100 full coverage, built hassio invocation, external settings wizard, and live all-format compact registry acceptance pass. Aggregate release and PM gates remain before publication."
  "2026-07-24T21:20:57.193Z",codex-root,PM full health identified tracked runtime cache sentinels as integrity drift. Removed the legacy search/locks .gitkeep files and obsolete negated ignore rules so runtime indexes and locks remain untracked while PM recreates directories as needed.
  "2026-07-24T21:27:13.270Z",codex-root,Latest-version recheck during release verification discovered pm-changelog 2026.7.24 had just become available; the managed package was refreshed from 2026.7.23 to 2026.7.24 and changelog check remains unchanged/clean for the 46 terminal items.
  "2026-07-24T21:30:19.691Z",codex-root,"The removed runtime sentinels are intentionally documented in this decision comment rather than retained as file links, because strict PM file validation correctly treats linked deleted paths as missing evidence."
  "2026-07-24T21:41:13.784Z",codex-root,"CI static-contracts exposed a clean-checkout-only PM invariant: ignored runtime directories do not exist after clone. The quality:pm entrypoint now creates locks/search immediately before strict validation, preserving untracked runtime state while making local and hosted health behavior identical; a static contract test prevents regression."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-24T21:01:24.761Z",codex-root,"Privacy boundary: keep token, credentials, raw live registry rows, user identifiers, signed paths, and instance inventory out of PM, git, logs, and GitHub."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-24T21:01:24.761Z",codex-root,Official Home Assistant docs now designate config/entity_registry/list_for_display as the bandwidth-efficient enabled-entity contract; the live server returns compact documented field keys.
